7.3 Ingestion & Validation Activity — ACT-003
Objective
Represent event-triggered ingestion with secure source access, schema validation, transformation, object persistence, catalog registration, and failure handling.
```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A([Observation notification received]) --> B[Validate event contract and publisher identity]
  B --> C{Valid and authorized?}
  C -->|No| D[Reject, audit, and quarantine event] --> END1([Rejected])
  C -->|Yes| E[Check event ID / ingestion idempotency key]
  E --> F{Previously processed?}
  F -->|Yes| G[Return prior receipt / no duplicate processing] --> END2([Duplicate handled])
  F -->|No| H[Retrieve source object with separate authorization]
  H --> I{Object available and authorized?}
  I -->|No| J[Retry or escalate per failure classification] --> END3([Pending / failed])
  I -->|Yes| K[Validate source schema and metadata]
  K --> L{Valid data?}
  L -->|No| M[Quarantine; record reason and provenance] --> END4([Rejected data])
  L -->|Yes| N[Normalize to canonical model]
  N --> O[Persist immutable or versioned data asset]
  O --> P[Register metadata in enterprise catalog]
  P --> Q{Registration committed?}
  Q -->|No| R[Reconcile and retry registration] --> P
  Q -->|Yes| S[Record lineage and publish asset-registered event]
  S --> T[Commit ingestion completion / checkpoint] --> END5([Available for workflows])
```
Ingestion acceptance examples
ID	Given	When	Then
AC-ING-01	Authorized source and conformant event	Event arrives	Ingestion creates a correlated receipt
AC-ING-02	Event ID already processed	Duplicate is delivered	No duplicate asset is created; prior outcome is retrievable
AC-ING-03	Data fails schema validation	Validation executes	Data is quarantined with a recorded reason
AC-ING-04	Object is stored but catalog registration fails	Reconciliation executes	Registration is retried without duplicating the stored object
AC-ING-05	Metadata registration succeeds	Registration transaction completes	A governed asset-registered event is published


Architectural caveat: Retry loops shown here are bounded by policy. After retry exhaustion, processing transitions to an exception or operator-reconciliation state rather than retrying indefinitely.
