7.5 Failure Handling & Recovery Activity — ACT-005
Failure taxonomy
Failure	Detection	Immediate response	Recovery / assurance
Invalid or unauthorized event	Schema and authorization check	Reject, audit	Correct producer contract or permission; do not auto-bypass
Duplicate event	Event ID/idempotency record	Return prior outcome	Confirm no duplicate side effects
Temporary source outage	Retrieval timeout / health signal	Retry with backoff	Resume from checkpoint or escalate
Transformation failure	Processor exception / invalid output	Quarantine input/output	Correct mapping; preserve evidence
Object stored, catalog unavailable	Registration failure	Mark asset not yet discoverable	Reconciliation and eventual registration
Event broker outage	Publish/subscribe health failure	Buffer through approved durable mechanism	Resume/replay; verify completeness
Analytical service timeout	Job deadline exceeded	Transition to exception state	Retry only if safe; otherwise operator decision
Policy decision unavailable	PDP / enforcement health failure	Deny protected action by default	Restore policy service; audit outage
Report release denied	Approval/recipient policy	Block dissemination	Request proper approval; retain record
Deployment regression	Health/SLO degradation	Stop rollout	Rollback to approved version; incident review


```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A([Failure detected]) --> B[Correlate event, workflow, and asset IDs]
  B --> C{Security or policy violation?}
  C -->|Yes| D[Fail closed; deny, preserve evidence, alert] --> END1([Security investigation])
  C -->|No| E{Transient and retry-safe?}
  E -->|Yes| F[Bounded retry with backoff]
  F --> G{Recovered?}
  G -->|Yes| H[Resume from checkpoint; validate integrity] --> END2([Recovered])
  G -->|No| I[Dead-letter / exception queue]
  E -->|No| I
  I --> J[Notify operator and record incident]
  J --> K{Approved manual recovery?}
  K -->|Yes| L[Reconcile state / controlled replay] --> H
  K -->|No| M[Retain failed state and evidence] --> END3([Await resolution])
```
Required recovery properties
- Idempotency: Duplicate messages or retried commands do not create unintended duplicate effects.
- Bounded retry: Timeouts, backoff, and maximum attempts are specified by interface.
- Checkpoints: Durable state enables resumption without restarting an entire mission workflow unnecessarily.
- Compensation: Where a multi-service action cannot be atomic, use explicit reconciliation or compensating steps.
- Auditability: Failure, intervention, and recovery actions retain traceable records.
- Fail-safe security: Unavailable policy enforcement does not authorize protected operations.
- Operational metrics: Recovery time and data completeness targets are defined and approved before verification.
7.6 Operational Sequence Diagrams
Sequence A — Collection to governed catalog registration
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Collection Adapter
  participant B as Event Broker
  participant I as Ingestion Service
  participant Z as Authorization
  participant O as Object Storage
  participant K as Data Catalog
  participant P as Provenance Service
  C->>B: Publish observation.available(event ID, asset reference)
  B-->>I: Deliver authorized subscription event
  I->>I: Validate envelope and deduplicate
  I->>Z: Authorize object retrieval
  Z-->>I: Permit / deny
  alt Authorized and valid
    I->>C: Retrieve authorized source payload
    C-->>I: Payload + source metadata
    I->>I: Validate and normalize
    I->>O: Store versioned object
    O-->>I: Object reference
    I->>K: Register metadata
    K-->>I: Registration committed
    I->>P: Record source / transformation lineage
    K->>B: Publish catalog.asset.registered
  else Denied or invalid
    I->>P: Record rejection evidence as authorized
    I-->>B: Negative outcome / controlled exception
  end
```
Sequence B — Mission task to analytical report
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor A as Mission Analyst
  participant M as Mission Application
  participant Z as Authorization
  participant K as Data Catalog
  participant W as Workflow Service
  participant N as Analytics Service
  participant R as Report Service
  A->>M: Submit analytical request
  M->>Z: Authorize task submission
  Z-->>M: Permit / deny
  M->>K: Discover authorized assets
  K-->>M: Governed asset references
  M->>W: Create workflow(template, asset IDs)
  W-->>M: Accepted + workflow ID
  W->>N: Dispatch analytical job
  N-->>W: Completion + result reference
  W->>R: Initiate draft report
  R-->>A: Present draft for review
  A->>R: Approve / request changes
  alt Approved and release authorized
    R->>R: Verify markings, recipients, release policy
    R-->>A: Dissemination receipt
  else Not approved
    R-->>A: Retain draft / request revision
  end
```
Sequence C — Deployment with rollback
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor E as Engineer
  participant G as Version Control / CI
  participant S as Security & Test Gates
  participant D as Deployment Controller
  participant O as Observability
  participant CM as Configuration Management
  E->>G: Submit approved change
  G->>S: Build artifact and run checks
  S-->>G: Test / scan results
  alt Gates pass
    G->>CM: Register approved version
    CM-->>D: Authorize controlled deployment
    D->>O: Deploy and observe release
    O-->>D: Health / performance indicators
    alt Healthy
      D-->>CM: Record successful deployment state
    else Degraded
      D->>D: Roll back to prior approved version
      D-->>CM: Record rollback and incident
    end
  else Gates fail
    G-->>E: Reject build; remediate
  end
```
State model for mission workflow
```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Submitted
  Submitted --> Rejected: authorization denied
  Submitted --> Accepted: authorized
  Accepted --> Running: resources ready
  Running --> Waiting: external dependency
  Waiting --> Running: dependency restored
  Running --> Completed: all required tasks pass
  Running --> Failed: unrecoverable error
  Running --> Cancelled: authorized cancellation
  Failed --> Running: approved controlled replay
  Completed --> [*]
  Rejected --> [*]
  Cancelled --> [*]
```
